{"items":[{"targetId":"n0000505","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Parallel reduction performs independent local reductions concurrently instead of choosing one sequential evaluation order.","densityScore":0.91,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the evaluation strategy named by the dependent claim."}]},{"targetId":"n0000506","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A net is a graph-like program representation made from connected agents or nodes with explicitly typed ports.","densityScore":0.89,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the computational structure used throughout the model."}]},{"targetId":"n0000507","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A graph is a collection of nodes connected by edges that represent relationships or data flow.","densityScore":0.96,"relation":"fills","reason":"Supplies the structural concept behind graph-based computation."}]},{"targetId":"n0000508","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Scope is the region of a program in which a variable binding is visible and may be referenced.","densityScore":0.95,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the binding boundary relevant to variables and abstractions."}]},{"targetId":"n0000509","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"An abstraction packages a computation while hiding selected implementation details behind an interface or binding structure.","densityScore":0.85,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the general concept used by lambda abstraction."}]},{"targetId":"n0000510","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A variable is a symbolic name whose occurrences refer to a value or to a binding introduced elsewhere.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the binding reference used in lambda terms."}]},{"targetId":"n0000511","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A lambda is the binder notation in lambda calculus that introduces a function parameter, as in λx. body.","densityScore":0.96,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the syntactic construct underlying lambda abstraction."}]},{"targetId":"n0000512","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Lambda calculus is a minimal formal system in which functions are built from variables, abstraction, and application.","densityScore":0.97,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the source language whose reductions are represented by nets."}]},{"targetId":"n0000513","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Variable distribution is the placement and routing of variable occurrences from one binding to every use that refers to it.","densityScore":0.82,"relation":"fills","reason":"Explains why a graph encoding must manage multiple uses of a bound variable."}]},{"targetId":"n0000514","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Depth is the number of nesting levels or edges separating an element from a chosen outer context or root.","densityScore":0.86,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the structural measure used for nested constructs."}]},{"targetId":"n0000515","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"An interaction net is a port graph whose agents rewrite locally when their principal ports are connected according to an interaction rule.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the formal graph-rewriting model at issue."}]},{"targetId":"n0000516","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A lambda abstraction is a function-forming expression λx. M that binds x within body M.","densityScore":0.98,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the lambda-calculus construct being encoded."}]},{"targetId":"n0000517","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"An interaction is a local computational event in which connected agents are eligible to be replaced by a rewrite rule.","densityScore":0.88,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the event that drives net reduction."}]},{"targetId":"n0000518","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A term is a syntactic expression built from the constructors of a formal language, such as variables, applications, and abstractions.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the source-level expression translated into a net."}]},{"targetId":"n0000519","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Substitution replaces free occurrences of a variable in an expression with another expression while preserving binding meaning.","densityScore":0.96,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the operation graph reduction is intended to realize."}]},{"targetId":"n0000520","injections":[{"type":"uncertainty","text":"A δ-net appears to be a net formalism centered on a δ agent, likely used to model duplication or sharing; its exact rule set depends on the source formalism.","densityScore":0.61,"relation":"fills","reason":"Provides a cautious prerequisite definition without asserting source-specific rules."}]},{"targetId":"n0000521","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A syntax tree is a rooted tree that represents how an expression is recursively composed from language constructors.","densityScore":0.96,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the tree representation contrasted with graphs."}]},{"targetId":"n0000522","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A substitution machine is an abstract evaluator that implements variable replacement through an explicit operational representation rather than direct textual rewriting.","densityScore":0.87,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the machine model used as a comparison point."}]},{"targetId":"n0000523","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Textual substitution rewrites an expression by replacing variable names in its written syntax with another expression.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the syntax-oriented alternative to graph-based substitution."}]},{"targetId":"n0000524","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A graph representation encodes a structure as nodes and explicit connections rather than as a nested textual or tree form.","densityScore":0.92,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the representation used to expose sharing and local rewrites."}]},{"targetId":"n0000525","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Graph rewriting transforms a graph by replacing a local matched subgraph with another graph according to a rule.","densityScore":0.97,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the computation mechanism used by nets."}]},{"targetId":"n0000526","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A node is an individual graph element that represents an entity, operation, or constructor and connects through edges or ports.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the basic unit of a net."}]},{"targetId":"n0000527","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A rewrite is one application of a transformation rule that replaces a matched local structure with its prescribed result.","densityScore":0.95,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines an individual reduction step."}]},{"targetId":"n0000528","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A reducible pattern is a local configuration that matches the left-hand side of a rewrite rule and can therefore be reduced.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the condition that makes a net region eligible for rewriting."}]},{"targetId":"n0000529","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A reduction sequence is an ordered chain of rewrite steps from an initial expression or net toward a later form.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the multi-step computation path."}]},{"targetId":"n0000530","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Graph-rewriting is computation by repeatedly applying local replacement rules to matched graph configurations.","densityScore":0.95,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the hyphenated form of the graph-rewriting concept."}]},{"targetId":"n0000531","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"An interaction rule specifies how a particular pair of interacting agents is replaced when their principal ports meet.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the rule governing each local interaction."}]},{"targetId":"n0000532","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A reduction path is a particular sequence of choices of reducible patterns and rewrites from one state to another.","densityScore":0.9,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines a specific route through possible reductions."}]},{"targetId":"n0000533","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Term-to-net translation maps a source term into a net whose connectivity represents the term's constructors, bindings, and variable uses.","densityScore":0.92,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the encoding direction from syntax to graph."}]},{"targetId":"n0000534","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Net-to-term translation reconstructs a source-language term from a net when the net has a structure corresponding to that language.","densityScore":0.87,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the decoding direction from graph to syntax."}]},{"targetId":"n0000535","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A principal-port interaction occurs when the distinguished principal ports of two agents are connected, triggering their interaction rule.","densityScore":0.96,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the exact local condition for interaction-net reduction."}]},{"targetId":"n0000536","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Arity is the number of auxiliary ports, arguments, or inputs associated with an agent or operation.","densityScore":0.94,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the structural property of agents."}]},{"targetId":"n0000537","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A rooted net is a net with a distinguished free port that identifies the whole computation's external result or entry point.","densityScore":0.85,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the designated interface of a net."}]},{"targetId":"n0000538","injections":[{"type":"uncertainty","text":"A canonical lambda encoding is a chosen standard translation from lambda terms to nets that preserves the intended binding and reduction behavior.","densityScore":0.73,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the phrase cautiously because canonicality depends on the formalism."}]},{"targetId":"n0000539","injections":[{"type":"uncertainty","text":"A delta interaction is an interaction involving a δ agent; in sharing-oriented net systems it commonly concerns duplication or distribution of connected structure.","densityScore":0.66,"relation":"fills","reason":"Provides a cautious source-formalism-dependent definition."}]},{"targetId":"n0000540","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A duplication context is the surrounding graph structure that determines what must be copied or distributed when a shared value is used more than once.","densityScore":0.82,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the context governing duplication behavior."}]},{"targetId":"n0000541","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"Nesting is the containment of one syntactic or graph structure inside another, producing hierarchical depth.","densityScore":0.91,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the structural relation needed for term-like interpretations."}]},{"targetId":"n0000542","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A term-like reading interprets a graph as if its connectivity expressed the hierarchical structure of a conventional syntactic term.","densityScore":0.85,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the interpretive bridge from nets back to terms."}]},{"targetId":"n0000543","injections":[{"type":"definition","text":"A teaching summary is a simplified explanatory account designed to make the main ideas and dependencies easier to learn.","densityScore":0.9,"relation":"fills","reason":"Defines the pedagogical artifact referenced by the dependent knowledge."}]},{"targetId":"n0000027","injections":[{"type":"mechanism","text":"Each rewrite acts only on a small local graph pattern, allowing independent patterns to be reduced without traversing the entire program.","densityScore":0.88,"relation":"elaborates","reason":"Explains why representing computation as local nodes and wires supports reduction."}]},{"targetId":"n0000028","injections":[{"type":"warrant","text":"Sharing represents one needed computation once and routes its result to multiple uses, avoiding repeated evaluation of the same expression.","densityScore":0.93,"relation":"supports","reason":"Explains the mechanism behind reducing necessary work once."}]}]}
